  concept: "Authored objective: Path A Forward Diode.\nAuthored requirement: With
    Switch A closed and Switch B open, verify D1 is forward biased. voltage \u2265
    0.45 V. voltage \u2264 1 V. Connection pair D_OR_A_Anode and D_OR_A_Cathode.\nGeneral
    teaching principle: Diode behavior depends on polarity, operating point and its
    device characteristics.\nOnly fresh, authoritative game evidence can establish
    that this objective is complete."
  analogy: A direction-sensitive valve is an approximation, not a complete semiconductor
    model.
  diagram: '[Authored setup] -> [Check prerequisites] -> [Observe the game evidence]
    -> [Verify objective]'
  misconception: Reverse bias and forward conduction must not be inferred from wire
    direction alone.
